Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2015 01:17:06 +0000
Subject: Difference in LOD between scanone and fitqtl
Message-ID: <WsOiG8zkx2g.ThpfFdo_AAAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/WsOiG8zkx2g/m/ThpfFdo_AAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello,

I got 2 QTL from scanone search, and got the LOD score (both 3.5) and the position of each QTL using lodint.
Then, with those positions, I performed makeqtl -> fitqtl. It indicated that the LOD scores of those QTL were 2.6. They are not as significant as they were indicated to be by scanone. There was no interaction between the two.

How come scanone and fitqtl give different LOD scores?

From u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com  Thu Aug 13 16:25:54 2015
From: u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com (Karl Broman)
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2015 16:25:54 +0000
Subject: Re: [Rqtl-disc] Difference in LOD between scanone and fitqtl
Message-ID: <WsOiG8zkx2g.aZg11S6jCgAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <WsOiG8zkx2g.ThpfFdo_AAAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <WsOiG8zkx2g.ThpfFdo_AAAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/WsOiG8zkx2g/m/aZg11S6jCgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The LOD scores from scanone compare a model with a single QTL to a model with no QTL.
The LOD scores in your use of fitqtl compare a model with two QTL to a model with one QTL.

So they tend to be different. fitqtl can give LOD scores that are either bigger or smaller; we hope for them to be bigger, but that doesn't always happen.

karl

