It's best not to treat an RIL population as an F2,
but R/qtl will omit any heterozygous genotypes in an RIL population.

When loading the data with read.cross, you can use the argument crosstype to indicate the cross type, either crosstype="risib" or crosstype="riself".

  mycross <- read.cross("csv", file="myfile.csv", crosstype="risib")

Alternatively, you can use the convert2riself() or convert2risib() functions

  mycross <- read.cross("csv", file="myfile.csv")
  mycross <- convert2risib(mycross)

karl

